 "reading": "The primary rule (T1) does not pass the pre-registered bar (failed: t2, holm, placebo). Out of sample: T1 +0.054R net (n 396, t +0.92; gross +0.105R, t +1.80; 2007-16 +0.005R, t +0.11; 34 of 40 placebos beaten; failed: t2, holm, placebo); T2 +0.032R net (n 494, t +0.38; gross +0.107R, t +1.27; 2007-16 +0.069R, t +0.94; 37 of 40 placebos beaten; failed: t2, holm, cost2x, placebo); T3 +0.111R net (n 231, t +1.47; gross +0.180R, t +2.37; 2007-16 +0.128R, t +1.96; 0 of 40 placebos beaten; failed: t2, holm, placebo). On weeks the median stop is $22.05 out of sample (18.41 in sample); costs and financing take 0.051R a trade on T1, of which financing 0.021R. The comparison (long every week from the open, same stop) made +0.084R a trade net out of sample (n 515, t +1.38) and −0.030R in sample. On T1 the buys made +0.135R a trade and the sells −0.040R out of sample, which is gold's rise more than the breakout. The placebo as pre-registered draws its entries from the weeks the test filled; for the buys-only T3 those are weeks in which price rose half a range above the open, so random buys earlier in the same week catch that rise (placebo median far above T3): a flaw of that placebo's design, said here and not repaired after the result; T3 fails on its t and Holm p in any case. Not an edge; nothing live changes and no proposal is written."
}
